    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="onb_title_1">Plug in the adapter</string>
    <string name="onb_text_1">Find the OBD2 port under the steering wheel (near the pedals) and plug the ELM327 adapter in. Then turn the ignition ON or start the engine.</string>
    <string name="onb_title_2">Pair it with your phone</string>
    <string name="onb_text_2">Open the phone Bluetooth settings and pair the adapter. Its name is usually OBDII, ELM327 or V-LINK. The common PIN is 1234 or 0000. (BLE adapters do not need pairing.)</string>
    <string name="onb_title_3">Connect in the app</string>
    <string name="onb_text_3">Tap the connection status at the top, pick your adapter and you are ready. No adapter yet? Try Demo mode to explore every screen.</string>
    <string name="onb_get_started">Get started</string>
    <string name="limits_note">Generic OBD2 reads the engine and emissions systems. ABS, airbags and transmission usually need brand-specific tools.</string>

